  "title": "India-Uzbekistan Strategic Partnership Deepens",
  "summary": "Prime Minister Narendra Modi and President Shavkat Mirziyoyev of Uzbekistan held delegation-level talks to strengthen trade, defense, and energy cooperation, with the two countries aiming to further their shared developmental vision of 'Viksit Bharat' and 'Yangi Uzbekistan'. India's growing involvement in the Brics has expanded.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "India and Uzbekistan inked 11 agreements for boosting engagement in several key sectors, including mining and tourism, and agreed to establish a framework for the long-term supply of Uranium from Uzbekistan to India.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The two nations elevated relations to a comprehensive strategic partnership and announced a pact for the supply of uranium.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
